                "entry_id": "f37f360e-396e-3177-b9cf-ae704ff2d930",
                "word": "rupestral",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "98f55cb9-a0fb-3010-b3d1-22778a247e01",
                        "entry_id": "f37f360e-396e-3177-b9cf-ae704ff2d930",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Made on or placed on rock surfaces."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "75076b93-28f7-42d9-8b79-331d07130bdd",
                                "sense_id": "98f55cb9-a0fb-3010-b3d1-22778a247e01",
                                "text": "Having departed from Sardis and before reaching the mnema of Tos, the traveller saw a monument which was either a free-standing pillar or a rupestral tablet, depending on how we interpret the word.^([στήλη])"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9031520c-eee2-4cfc-9a2c-63c0152526be",
                                "sense_id": "98f55cb9-a0fb-3010-b3d1-22778a247e01",
                                "text": "In the course of the last decade, a fair number of ancient rupestral (rock-cut) horoi have been published from various sites in southern Attica."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ad0fc92-6632-4199-95cc-ecf72cb8d5ce",
                                "sense_id": "98f55cb9-a0fb-3010-b3d1-22778a247e01",
                                "text": "Representational art appears in two major categories: rupestral art (as in the paintings of the Palaeolithic caves) and mobiliary art (also called mobile or portable art)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c28b3342-6f05-310a-8716-d6100a2aa75b",
                        "entry_id": "f37f360e-396e-3177-b9cf-ae704ff2d930",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Constructed in rock; made of rock."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "29d0b368-1f1a-4e34-8b62-f3cc22931e5f",
                                "sense_id": "c28b3342-6f05-310a-8716-d6100a2aa75b",
                                "text": "On the north side of the city, just outside the wall, the rupestral sanctuary of S. Biagio consists of a series of artificial caves or tunnels in the rocky hillside."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b4580a82-8d9c-4d3b-84f5-78e6dc23994a",
                                "sense_id": "c28b3342-6f05-310a-8716-d6100a2aa75b",
                                "text": "2011, Ömür Harmaşah, 28: Monuments an Memory: Architecture and Visual Culture in Ancient Anatolian History, Sharon R. Steadman, Gregory McMahon (editors), The Oxford Handbook of Ancient Anatolia: (10,000-323 BCE), page 643,\nThe sculpted and columnar rupestral tombs of Achaemenid Paphlagonia, the mountainous Black Sea region west of the Halys (Kızıl Irmak), are equally fascinating in their place-making qualities and their deliberate use of the living rock."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "de58f73d-7acf-396a-a084-c7eebe1d42dd",
                        "entry_id": "f37f360e-396e-3177-b9cf-ae704ff2d930",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Growing on rocks."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bce8fb4e-c872-4579-bfd7-71713b270bab",
                                "sense_id": "de58f73d-7acf-396a-a084-c7eebe1d42dd",
                                "text": "The rupestral species have been the next class of lichens to suffer from the atmospheric pollution; and the effects are particularly noticeable in the hilly districts in the eastern part of South Lancashire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "73b90cad-cd86-4dff-b5c3-2df5d750b68d",
                                "sense_id": "de58f73d-7acf-396a-a084-c7eebe1d42dd",
                                "text": "By contrast, in the oak woodland on a steep hillside at Keskadale in Cumberland the occurrence is solely rupestral."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "895aa09b-4bdc-4163-8c56-3690fdf38e82",
                                "sense_id": "de58f73d-7acf-396a-a084-c7eebe1d42dd",
                                "text": "Among the more notable of these rupestral oceanic and Atlantic bryophytes of acidic rocks are the mosses[…]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
